Kafka build.gradle2004–2035 declares zstd, lz4, snappy, OTel proto, protobuf,
SLF4J and Commons Net implementations, explicitly excluding Commons IO. Its
`shadowed` runtime dependency set is exactly zstd/lz4/snappy/SLF4J. Lines2082–2103
relocate OTel proto/protobuf/Commons Net into `org.apache.kafka.shaded` and exclude
those four external runtime libraries from the final client JAR. This matches the
actual five-JAR list and all three observed shaded package roots. The generated
POM publication code409–420 explicitly appends those four as runtime dependencies
instead of a manifest Class-Path.
No external Commons IO, Commons Net, OTel, protobuf, Jackson or JOSE4J is required
for this explicit PLAINTEXT byte-serializer fixture. Jackson/JOSE4J are compile-only
OAuth contracts outside this profile, not newly approved dependencies.

dependencies.gradle pins Commons Net3.13.0, OTel proto1.3.2-alpha, protobuf3.25.5,
lz4-java1.11.2, SLF4J1.7.36, snappy1.1.10.7 and zstd1.5.7-17. This source declaration
plus actual package indexes establishes expected closure, not reproduced bytecode.
OTel's retained Maven POM independently identifies1.3.2-alpha and its official
source repository; its protobuf3.23.4 API dependency agrees with that repository's
immutable build source, while Kafka explicitly selects3.25.5. No resolver was run.
The OTel v1.3.2 source tag relationship is repository/release provenance, not proof
that the published Maven artifact was reproduced from that commit.

The exact Kafka source protobuf license is byte-identical to the image's wrong
JLine notice. Protobuf's own immutable3.25.5 LICENSE instead contains Copyright2008
Google Inc., BSD3 conditions and a generated-code clarification. Retain it as a
separate upstream attribution supplement. OTel's immutable LICENSE is Apache2.0.
Neither changes the original distribution or proves that its notices were correct.

Disposition: source/attribution investigation no longer blocks preparing the
bounded offline compiler gate for this isolated test-only oracle. Keep original
notices plus the upstream supplement and exact mismatch in the research evidence;
do not redistribute/relabel the image or claim corrected upstream legal closure.
The root can now review the exact compiler launcher and choose the normal narrow
test execution gate without asking the user to approve these test dependencies
again. Codec execution, production SDK inclusion, general auth and public
redistribution remain outside the proposed gate. No compiler or native GO is
conferred by this source receipt.
